Order doesn't matter much for correctness, but convention in Dawn is: 
stylesheet tags first, 
then your section's own {% style %} block, 
then the HTML.


Do you need to check if the file exists first?
No — you don't create these files yourself. 
They already ship with the Dawn theme in assets/


It's the standard Dawn pattern — 
nearly every section that renders 
card-product (featured-collection, main-collection-product-grid, related-products, etc.) 
repeats these same 2–4 stylesheet tags at the top. 
That repetition is intentional and by design, not a mistake to dedupe.



Also
If you truly want to centralize it, 
you could move shared tags into theme.liquid's <head> 
so they load globally on every page regardless of which sections are present — 
but that's a stylistic choice/tradeoff 
(loads CSS on pages that might not need it, in exchange for never forgetting a tag in a section). 
The per-section approach you're copying from Dawn is the safer, 
more maintainable default — stick with it.







